# Yaw threshold -- where between 96 and 127 does the stick start turning?
#
# The sweep (yaw-sweep.pad) found the camera turning at 2.10 deg/frame at full
# deflection and not at all at 96 or below: 0.0000 deg across 367 objects in
# every window. Either the game thresholds the stick near the rim and turns
# digitally above it, or the AC stopped being controllable around poll 2290
# and the sweep, which dumped no frames, could not see it. This run holds
# 127, 120, 112, 104, 100 and 96 on both sides and dumps frames, so it answers
# both.
#
# It also takes RAM snapshots for scripts/ram-diff.py during the first hold:
# polls 2104-2107, inside the camera's ramp-up, where the AC's own heading
# should step by a constant while the camera's yaw does not -- which is what
# tells the two variables apart -- and 2130-2133 in the steady state, where
# both step by the same amount.
#
#   scripts/09-replay.sh --decode \
#     --env PSPRECOMP_VIEW_LOG=reports/yaw-threshold.view \
#     --env PSPRECOMP_VIEW_LOG_WORLD=all \
#     --env PSPRECOMP_VIEW_LOG_POLLS=2098-2110,2158-2170,2210-2215,2290-2295,2370-2375,2450-2455,2530-2535,2610-2615,2690-2695,2770-2775,2850-2855,2930-2935,3010-3015 \
#     --env PSPRECOMP_RAMSNAP=reports/snap \
#     --env PSPRECOMP_RAMSNAP_POLLS=2104,2105,2106,2107,2130,2131,2132,2133 \
#     --env PSPRECOMP_FRAMES=reports/thr-frames --env PSPRECOMP_FRAMES_EVERY=100 \
#     scenarios/yaw-threshold.pad

